      "text": [
        " : أَهْدَى فَيْضُ بْنُ اَلْمُخْتَارِ إِلَى أَبِي عَبْدِ اَللَّهِ عَلَيْهِ اَلسَّلاَمُ رَبِيثَا فَأَدْخَلَهَا إِلَيْهِ وَ أَنَا عِنْدَهُ فَنَظَرَ إِلَيْهَا وَ قَالَ \"هَذِهِ لَهَا قِشْرٌ\" فَأَكَلَ مِنْهَا وَ نَحْنُ نَرَاهُ."
      ],
      "translations": {
        "en.bab-ul-qaim-publications": [
          "Hadith.4205 - It is narrated from Hanan ibn Sadir who said:\n\"Fayd ibn Al-Mukhtar gifted a rabbit (al-rabitha) to Abu Abdullah (as). He brought it to him while I was present.\nImam (as) looked at it and said: \"This has a shell (skin),\" and Imam (as) ate from it while we were observing."
        ]
      }
